          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فوت کردن (fowt kardan) — \"to die (formal), to pass on\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "همسایه ما دیروز فوت کرد. Hamsâye-ye mâ diruz fowt kard. Our neighbour died yesterday."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neutral and polite, common in notices. Present fowt mikonad; the noun fowt is \"a death\". Spelled the same, fut kardan \"to blow\" is a different word."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fowt \"death, a passing\" is usually traced to Arabic fawt, \"a passing, a loss\"; EtymDB lists no entry. kardan \"to do\" is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
